          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          No. einvoiceops provides operational readiness support - structured work packets, action sequences, and accountability frameworks. We do not interpret tax law, give compliance opinions, or confirm that your organisation is compliant. All work packets are source-linked to official government and regulatory sources and include a clear disclaimer. For legal or tax interpretation, you need a qualified advisor. What we do is translate the operational implications of mandates into actions for the right people inside your organisation.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          What exactly do I receive at the end of a sprint?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          A set of structured work packets - one per relevant persona in your finance function (Finance Systems Owner, Tax/Compliance, Finance Ops). Each packet covers: mandate snapshot and what it means operationally, a T-minus action sequence from now to the deadline, fields and systems affected, what you need from other teams, and a partner accountability module with structured questions for your local accounting partners. Everything is source-linked with a confidence level and a snapshot date.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          My AP vendor says they already cover this. Why do I need a readiness sprint?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          Platform vendors handle the technical exchange layer - sending and receiving invoices in the right format. They do not handle what needs to happen inside your organisation before that works: master data quality (SIRET for France, GTU codes for Poland), internal ownership clarity, ERP connector configuration, exception handling processes, and partner confirmation across your local entities. These are internal readiness tasks your platform vendor cannot do for you. The sprint covers the gap between what your vendor delivers and what your organisation needs to have ready.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          How do you price the sprint?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          Fixed fee per sprint - one mandate, one country, one legal entity. Pricing is deliverable-based, not day-rate based: 50% on engagement start, 50% on delivery of the final work packet set. This keeps scope clean and predictable. Pricing is discussed directly before any engagement starts - get in touch with your situation and we will give you a clear number.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          We have multiple countries with upcoming mandates. Where do we start?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          Start with the nearest hard deadline. France (Sept 2026) and Poland (live) are the most time-pressured for most European groups right now. Germany issuance (Jan 2027) has a longer runway but a more complex internal preparation requirement. We can help you triage based on your entity footprint and ERP setup - send us a short note.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Do you work with companies of any size?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          The sprint is designed for companies with 500 to 5,000 employees operating across 3 to 20 EU countries. Large enough to have multi-country mandate exposure, lean enough that no single team has the bandwidth to own all of it. If you are smaller with only one country in scope, or larger with a dedicated compliance programme, the sprint may not be the right fit - and we will tell you that directly.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

